ulated no mercy breaking the windows  of those rooms knowing that those  students are sitting there  and are afraid for their lives and he's  just shooting them all and the fact that  after he leaves he throws the gun down  he knows he's guilty it doesn't show  mental illness it shows that he knows  he's guilty he throws the gun down he  goes to a mcdonald's and he goes and he  orders food and drink and he's talking  to someone like nothing ever happened no  question about it this man definitely  has mental issues but is cold calculated  and premeditated and when we come back  week two comes to a close in the  parkland school shooter penalty phase  trial hear testimony from the man who  sold the gunman his weapon and the uber  driver who dropped him off at the high  school  [Music]  back as the parkland school shooter  penalty phase trial stretched into its  second week jurors heard even more  testimony from shooting survivors  i was in fourth period um just sitting  there writing an essay and then  heard loud sounds like the gunshots and  then  everyone began to run in the classroom  um i had ran towards the back towards  the teacher's desk  and  i was on the ground uh  i had my hand and i was crawling against  around the ground  okay and then what happened and then um  we sat there for about  20 minutes or less than 20 minutes  probably and then um  the police had came into our classroom  and escorted us out  did you get shot yes all right when did  you get shot and where did you get shot  um when i was sitting or sitting or  running towards the back of the room in  my right arm in my lower right back okay  so what what happened as a result of  your injuries  um i have a couple fragments still in my  lower back and then um i have a scar on  my arm as well  jurors later heard from laura zucchini  the uber driver who dropped the shooter  off at marjory stoneman douglas high  school  i picked him up and he comes in the car  and he told me and he told me  he was going