ommit his crime so it all  kind of is pieces in the puzzle that the  prosecution is laying out  right we know that he had google  searches for the type of weapon ar-15s  he was searching for soft guitar case  very things that you saw there on the  video the weapon you heard the uber  driver talk about how he carried the  weapon into the school now terry the  prosecution is expected to rest its case  sometime next week but the trial is  expected to last for months what can we  expect going forward  well you know it's a very good question  because you would think that the  prosecution would have many more  witnesses but i do think that the  defense is going to put on a lot of  witnesses and the prosecution will be  cross-examining those witnesses and  it'll be two types of witnesses one to  talk about the mental health of the  defendant and two to talk about his  difficult childhood so i'm expecting  that we will see multiple medical  experts talking about his mental health  or the lack thereof they're going to be  pointing to like you said mike those  searches on the computer to indicate the  fact that he is having some mental  difficulty and as far as his childhood  is concerned he did not know his birth  parents he was adopted at birth and his  brother was also adopted at a very young  age and then ultimately his adopted  parents passed away when he was  relatively young and i'm certain that  the defense is going to bring some of  that in and there's also a video of the  brother who is saying to the defendant i  love you no matter what i'm here for you  so that will be shown as a matter of  life and death for nicholas cruz life  behind bars or going to the death  chamber thank you for joining us here on  law and crime daily we'll see you next  time as we discuss justice in america  [Music]  [Music]  you

